{"content":[{"c":["PEREZ, PEREZITE"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Son of Judah whose name is derived from a Hebrew word meaning “he who bursts forth”; his name refers to the manner in which he unexpectedly came first from Tamar’s womb before his twin brother, Zerah (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.38.29","r":"Gen.38.29","rawR":"Gen.38.29","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.38.29","value":"Gen.38.29"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 38:29"},"). He fathered two sons, Hezron and Hamul, and became the ancestral head of the Perezite family (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.46.12","r":"Gen.46.12","rawR":"Gen.46.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.46.12","value":"Gen.46.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 46:12"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Num.26.20-21","r":"Num.26.20-21","rawR":"Num.26.20-21","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.26.20-21","value":"Num.26.20-21"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 26:20-21"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.2.4-5","r":"1Chr.2.4-5","rawR":"1Chr.2.4-5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.2.4-5","value":"1Chr.2.4-5"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 2:4-5"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.4.1","r":"1Chr.4.1","rawR":"1Chr.4.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.4.1","value":"1Chr.4.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"4:1"},"). The ",{"c":["kjv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"}," and the Apocrypha translate the name variously as Pharez, Phares, and Pharzite."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":["Through the descent of his son Hezron, he became the ancestor of David and Jesus Christ (",{"href":"?bref=Ruth.4.18-22","r":"Ruth.4.18-22","rawR":"Ruth.4.18-22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ruth.4.18-22","value":"Ruth.4.18-22"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ru 4:18-22"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Matt.1.3","r":"Matt.1.3","rawR":"Matt.1.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.1.3","value":"Matt.1.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mt 1:3"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Luke.3.33","r":"Luke.3.33","rawR":"Luke.3.33","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Luke.3.33","value":"Luke.3.33"}],"t":"ref","v":"Lk 3:33"},"). The esteem this clan enjoyed in the tribe of Judah is evidenced by the blessing pronounced upon it by the men of Bethlehem (",{"href":"?bref=Ruth.4.12","r":"Ruth.4.12","rawR":"Ruth.4.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ruth.4.12","value":"Ruth.4.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ru 4:12"},"). A descendant named Jashobeam commanded David’s captains for the first month of each year (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.27.2-3","r":"1Chr.27.2-3","rawR":"1Chr.27.2-3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.27.2-3","value":"1Chr.27.2-3"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 27:2-3"},"). Upon the return from captivity in Babylon, 468 Perezites were chosen to live in Jerusalem (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.9.4","r":"1Chr.9.4","rawR":"1Chr.9.4","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.9.4","value":"1Chr.9.4"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 9:4"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Neh.11.4-6","r":"Neh.11.4-6","rawR":"Neh.11.4-6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Neh.11.4-6","value":"Neh.11.4-6"}],"t":"ref","v":"Neh 11:4-6"},")."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"PerezPerezite","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Gn 38:29","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.38.29","rawQueryValue":"Gen.38.29","sourceRefExact":"Gen.38.29"},{"anchorText":"Gn 46:12","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.46.12","rawQueryValue":"Gen.46.12","sourceRefExact":"Gen.46.12"},{"anchorText":"Nm 26:20-21","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.26.20-21","rawQueryValue":"Num.26.20-21","sourceRefExact":"Num.26.20-21"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 2:4-5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.2.4-5","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.2.4-5","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.2.4-5"},{"anchorText":"4:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.4.1","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.4.1","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.4.1"},{"anchorText":"Ru 4:18-22","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ruth.4.18-22","rawQueryValue":"Ruth.4.18-22","sourceRefExact":"Ruth.4.18-22"},{"anchorText":"Mt 1:3","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Matt.1.3","rawQueryValue":"Matt.1.3","sourceRefExact":"Matt.1.3"},{"anchorText":"Lk 3:33","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Luke.3.33","rawQueryValue":"Luke.3.33","sourceRefExact":"Luke.3.33"},{"anchorText":"Ru 4:12","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ruth.4.12","rawQueryValue":"Ruth.4.12","sourceRefExact":"Ruth.4.12"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 27:2-3","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.27.2-3","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.27.2-3","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.27.2-3"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 9:4","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.9.4","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.9.4","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.9.4"},{"anchorText":"Neh 11:4-6","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Neh.11.4-6","rawQueryValue":"Neh.11.4-6","sourceRefExact":"Neh.11.4-6"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"2a2db1d41353fdcbc6b817f2f1ae6ac06e1ef34f958cb60df922bdfcb6d6c367","sourceItemName":"PerezPerezite","sourceItemOrder":119,"sourceMember":"Articles/P.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"PerezPerezite","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Perez, Perezite","title":"Perez, Perezite","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}